t two failures. `tests/session/test_env_completer.py::test_register_env_select_attaches_completer` failed because the argcomplete `completer` attribute is missing. `tests/session/cmd/test_schema.py::test_schema_tombi_lint[tox.toml]` errored, apparently on the tombi lint step. Neither touches `set_env`. I didn't check whether they also fail on the base commit, and the run stopped there, so the rest of `tests` outside `tests/config` didn't run.\n\nThe code changes are in the six files the spec lists.\n\nOne place goes beyond the spec text. For an INI reference to an overridden `set_env` whose base value is emptied by factor filtering (`win: MAGIC=base` on Linux), I treat the base as empty and still apply the override. The spec says a `KeyError` from `process_raw` gives `\"\"`, but `test_set_env_override_reference_appends_to_filtered_base` needs `MAGIC=appended` to survive. Without a `set_env` override, an emptied value still returns `\"\"` as before.\n\nNothing is committed.", "ttft_ms": 2573, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 263184, "uuid": "72bce258-9d3d-47dd-9b9c-5bde5955133f", "ttft_stream_ms": 2089, "time_to_request_ms": 51, "first_content_frame_ms": 2089, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
